  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SAC IV</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will support three key objectives:  (a) participatory articlation and implementation of a strategy for poverty redcution; (b) implementation of public expenditrue programs in key poverty reduction sectors, underpinned by increased donor coordination and shared goals for poverty reduction; and, (c) increased efficiency, transparency and accountability of public resource management.   The project will support three key activities; (a) a more streamlined role of the State and increased participation of beneficiaries to policy formulation, financiing, and delivery of public services; (b) increased impact ofpublic expenditures on poverty reduction by basing allocation of public resources on a comprehensivedatabase on poverty and development, and monitoring poverty outcomes; (c) enhanced efficiency and sustainability of poverty reduction through improved public resource management and generation of public savings. T he decision meeting will determine whether this project will be a single operation disbursed in three tranches or three single tranche operations for a total amount of $60 million dollars.</narrative>
  </description>
